      answer: 1,
      why: 'Both genres have a viewpoint — the difference is the contract with the reader. The analyst\'s obligation is to the strength of the evidence: a thesis that survives counter-evidence, and sourcing the reader can check. The columnist\'s obligation is to make the strongest honest case for a position. The label tells the reader which contract applies.',
    },
