        'A wire story',
      ],
      answer: 1,
      why: 'Sponsored content borrows the credibility the newsroom spent years building — that is precisely its business model. Regulators (the FTC in the US, the ASA in the UK) require clear disclosure, and serious outlets keep such work out of newsroom typography or label it loudly. The genre distinction exists to protect exactly this judgement.',
